      "reason": "Processing schema 8 migrates atomically to schema 9 for bounded scalar manifest ledgers (#1766). The combined processing-9/automation-4 boundary bc5ca7489c4090c299c416309519ab72da4a8cdb carries that migration signal from the processing-only boundary 4293871b7c4cf38ce0e0e4ea969aa9a6de057eea. Schema 10 added the retained astrometry partial index (#1901, released by PR #1902). The shared schema 12 boundary introduced the scheduler calendar and availability observations (#1921) and retained view tables (#1922). Publisher activation reused that boundary. The combined schema 12 follow-up adds the publication deadline index, registration input failure table (#1961), and six centered-view retention indexes (#2000). The distinct minimum-compatible-revision selects the paired checkpoint before startup when upgrading from either predecessor, even when raw schema is already 17. Rollback restores the previous reader's raw journal and processing evidence from that checkpoint. Frozen SQL images remain unchanged."
